\b STI-FORECAST Application Outline\b0\par
\par
\b 1. Purpose and Scope\b0\par
- Provide a professional outbreak intelligence platform for monitoring, analysis, forecasting, and decision support.\par
- Combine real public datasets (OWID) with simulated operational outbreak signals for rapid prototyping and planning.\par
\par
\b 2. Current Key Functionalities\b0\par
\b 2.1 Landing Experience\b0\par
- Professional landing page with motion background and feature overview.\par
- Quick-action navigation buttons into key modules.\par
\par
\b 2.2 Dashboard and Monitoring\b0\par
- Live outbreak dashboard with key metrics (cholera, malaria, affected countries, news signals).\par
- Trend controls, alert prioritization, hotspot map, and dynamic signal intensity scoring.\par
- Manual and automated refresh controls.\par
\par
\b 2.3 Feed Reliability and Operations\b0\par
- Retry/backoff feed loading strategy.\par
- Per-feed health states (OK / Degraded / Unavailable).\par
- Fallback snapshots when live APIs fail.\par
- Per-feed diagnostics: last success, latency, retries, last error.\par
\par
\b 2.4 Disease Intelligence Modules\b0\par
- Disease Explorer (cholera, malaria, typhoid context and age profile visualization).\par
- Region Watch for district-level simulated surveillance.\par
- Alerts and Recommendations module with 72-hour operational checklist.\par
\par
\b 2.5 Forecasting and Planning\b0\par
- Forecast Lab for intervention vs no-control scenario projection.\par
- ROI and Financing module for preparedness investment impact modeling.\par
\par
\b 2.6 Global View\b0\par
- Combined global page showing:\par
  * Cholera (simulated international watchlist map)\par
  * Malaria Uganda real trend view\par
  * COVID-19 OWID global map and metrics\par
\par
\b 3. User Experience Enhancements Implemented\b0\par
- Professional button behaviors and unified navigation patterns.\par
- Sidebar branding with logo placement.\par
- Animated background for modern visual identity.\par
- Improved layout hierarchy and clarity across modules.\par
\par
\b 4. Technical Architecture (Current)\b0\par
- app.py: entrypoint, shared state, sidebar shell, main routing.\par
- data_services.py: external feed loading and resilient data retrieval.\par
- app_pages.py: modular page rendering components.\par
\par
\b 5. Recommended Future Integrations\b0\par
- WHO GHO OData for cholera and malaria indicators.\par
- DHIS2 / Ministry of Health district reporting APIs.\par
- Africa CDC / national public health event feeds.\par
- Optional alerting channels (email, SMS, Slack, Teams).\par
\par
\b 6. Recommended Next Technical Improvements\b0\par
- Add authentication and role-based access (analyst, manager, admin).\par
- Add persistent database layer (PostgreSQL) and ETL pipelines.\par
- Add audit logging for critical actions and configuration changes.\par
- Add testing suite (unit tests, integration tests, data contract tests).\par
\par
\b 7. Operational Value Summary\b0\par
- Faster situational awareness.\par
- Better intervention prioritization.\par
- More resilient data operations under partial feed failures.\par
- Stronger planning support for health response and investment decisions.\par
}
